lesson: 74
title: Some go away: how many went, how many at first
stars: 0
explain: In a story where some things go away we know two of three numbers: how many at first, how many went, how many are left.
explain: If the start and the rest are known, the ones that went are the start take away the rest: 20 at first, 13 left, so 20 - 13 = 7 went.
explain: If the ones that went and the rest are known, the start is the rest and the ones that went put back together: 7 went, 13 left, so 13 + 7 = 20 at first.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing x=5..60 p=2..40
need: x - p >= 2
answer: x
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}. {a.He} gave some to {b}. Now {a.he} has {p} {t}. How many {t} did {a.he} give to {b}?
exercise: There were {x+p} {t} in a box. {a} took some out. Now there are {p} {t} in the box. How many {t} did {a} take?
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}. {a.He} lost some. Now {a.he} has {p}. How many {t} did {a.he} lose?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {a.He} gave {p} {t} to {b}. Now {a.he} has {x-p} {t}. How many {t} did {a} have at first?
exercise: There were some {t} in a bag. {a} took {p} out. Now there are {x-p} {t} in the bag. How many {t} were in the bag at first?
exercise: A shop had some {t}. It sold {p} {t} and has {x-p} {t} left. How many {t} did the shop have at the start?
test: {p} {t} are left of the {x+p} that {a} once had. How many are gone?
test: {a} handed {p} {t} to {b} and kept the other {x-p}. How many {t} were there before {a} shared?
test: After some {t} rolled off the table, {p} of the {x+p} were still on it. How many {t} rolled off?
test: {x-p} {t} are still in the jar after {a} took out {p}. How many {t} were in the jar to begin with?
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}. After giving some away, {a.he} has {p} left. How many {t} did {a.he} give away?
exercise: How many {t} did {a} lose? {a.He} had {x+p} and now has {p}.
exercise: A shop in Vermont had {x+p} {t}. After a busy morning it has {p} {t} left. How many {t} did it sell?
exercise: {x+p} people were at a party in Brighton. Some went home, and {p} are still there. How many went home?
exercise: {a} donated {p} {t} to a school and has {x-p} {t} left. How many {t} did {a} have before donating?
exercise: There were some birds on a roof in Auckland. {p} flew away and {x-p} are still there. How many birds were on the roof at first?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. After handing out {p.words}, {a.he} still has {x-p}. How many did {a.he} have at the start?
exercise: {b} had {x+p} {t}. {b} gave some to {a} and kept {p}. How many {t} did {a} get?
test: A Toronto bakery ended the day with {p} of its {x+p} muffins. How many muffins were sold?
test: What must be taken from {x+p} to leave {p}?
test: After {a} gave {b} {p} {t}, {a} had {x-p} left. How many {t} did {a} have beforehand?
test: {p} sheep left a field in Kerry, and {x-p} sheep remained. How many sheep were in the field before?
test: A jar held {x+p} {t}; now only {p} remain in it. How many {t} were removed?
test: {a} spent {p} dollars at a fair in Iowa and has {x-p} dollars left. How many dollars did {a.he} bring?
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}, gave some to {b}, now {a.he}'s got {p}. how many {a.he} give
exercise: {x+p} {t} in the box, {a} took some, now {p} left. how many {a} take
exercise: {a} had some {t}, gave {p+1} — no wait, {p} — to {b}, now got {x-p}. how many at first
exercise: {a} had {x+p} {t}, lost some, now {p}. Kai says {a.he} lost {x+p+p}. nah, how many really
test: {a} gave {b} some of {a.his} {x+p} {t}, {p} left. how many went to {b}
test: some {t} in the bag, {a} took out {p}, {x-p} still in, oh and the bag's from 2019. how many to start
test: {a} lost {p} {t} and has {x-p} left. how many {a.he} had before
exam: Whereas {a} originally held {x+p} {t} and, following a transfer to {b}, retains {p}, determine the quantity transferred.
exam: It is given that a receptacle formerly containing {x+p} {t} now contains {p} {t}. Ascertain the number of {t} withdrawn in the interim.
exam: It is given that {a}, having disposed of {p} {t}, retains {x-p}. State the quantity of {t} originally in {a}'s possession.
exam: Determine the quantity which, when subtracted from {x+p}, leaves {p.words}.
exercise: The pet shop had {x+p} goldfish on Friday. Over the hot weekend some went to the big pond in the sky, and now there are {p}. How many goldfish died?
exercise: The factory had {x+p} workers. After a 'headcount reduction' it has {p}. How many workers were let go?
test: {a} swore {a.he} only ate a couple — total porkies. there were {x+p} biscuits in the tin, now there's {p}. how many did the greedy sod scoff
